  <title id="bdl20hybridsampling-title">Prior-initialized, optimization-initialized, single-chain and multi-chain sampling of the posterior of f(x) = w1 w2 x</title>
  <desc id="bdl20hybridsampling-desc">Five square panels with axes w1 and w2 from about −3 to 3. In the sample panels a thin black line marks the symmetry manifold w1 w2 = 1, two hyperbola branches in the upper-right and lower-left quadrants. Upper left: 40 time steps of a chain started far out on the upper-right branch near w1 = 3; the dots, dark for early and light for late steps, drift only slowly along the branch toward the mode at (1, 1). Upper right: 40 time steps of a chain started at the optimum (1, 1); the dots stay around the mode. A legend maps shading to time steps 10 to 40. Bottom left: the ground-truth posterior density, two curved bands of high density along both hyperbola branches, brightest near (1, 1) and (−1, −1). Bottom centre: a long single chain started at (1, 1) covers the upper-right band only and never reaches the lower-left one. Bottom right: two chains started at the two optimized points (1, 1) and (−1, −1) cover both bands.</desc>
